{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-007","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"material","page":1,"quote":"Polyurethene"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"HARDENED 40-45 HRC"}],"comment":"The title block specifies the material as \"Polyurethene\" but also calls for \"HARDENED 40-45 HRC\"; polyurethane is a polymer that cannot be heat-treated to a Rockwell C hardness, creating a direct contradiction. The designer must remove the impossible heat treatment callout or correct the material if a hardenable metal was intended."
    ,
    "recommended_correction": "Remove the heat treatment field or change the material to one that can achieve 40-45 HRC."}]}
